    "objective": "Operators report the plant is behaving abnormally, but no specific cause or location has been identified. Investigate across the process -- discover what equipment and measurements exist, check for deviations, and determine which equipment is actually affected and why.\n",
    "conclusion": "The plant is experiencing a gradual decline in temperatures across the downstream separation process. While the reactor temperature remained stable around 120.4 degC, the separator temperature decreased from 80.6 degC (01:00) to 76.1 degC (05:00), and the stripper temperature decreased from 66.1 degC (01:00) to 60.9 degC (05:00). This cooling trend is associated with a corresponding increase in the concentration of G in the stripper underflow, which rose from 53.9 mol % (01:00) to 55.9 mol % (05:00). The affected equipment are the separator and the stripper.",
